    </div>
    <div class="mt-faq-list">
      <div class="mt-faq-item open"><button class="mt-faq-q">Is Motilli safe with Ozempic, Mounjaro, Wegovy, or Zepbound?</button><div class="mt-faq-a"><p style="padding-top:4px;">Yes. Motilli's ingredients (celery juice extract / apigenin, sodium copper chlorophyllin, FOS, and whole-food vitamins) are non-pharmaceutical and don't interact with GLP-1 receptor agonists. Motilli is built specifically to counteract the side effects these drugs cause — not to interfere with the drugs themselves.</p></div></div>
      <div class="mt-faq-item mt-faq-item--tall"><button class="mt-faq-q">What's actually in Motilli?</button><div class="mt-faq-a"><div style="padding-top:4px;"><p style="margin:0 0 12px;">Motilli contains four active ingredients, each chosen for a specific role:</p><ul style="margin:0 0 12px; padding-left:20px;"><li style="margin-bottom:8px;"><strong>Apigenin (from cold-pressed celery juice extract)</strong> — A natural prokinetic flavonoid that helps wake up the smooth muscle in your stomach wall, restoring the gastric contraction signal that GLP-1 medications suppress.</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px;"><strong>Sodium Copper Chlorophyllin</strong> — A stabilized form of chlorophyll that binds to hydrogen sulfide and other sulfur compounds produced by bacterial fermentation in a slowed stomach. Neutralizes rotten-egg burps at the molecular source, not just the smell.</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px;"><strong>FOS Prebiotic Fiber (5g per serving)</strong> — A low-bulk soluble fiber that supports downstream colon transit without adding mass to an already-bloated stomach. Gentle, no cramping, no urgency.</li><li style="margin-bottom:8px;"><strong>Vitamins A, C, B6, K1, and Folate (whole-food sourced)</strong> — Replaces the key nutrients GLP-1 users typically lose from eating 30% less than they used to. Sourced from whole-food extracts, not synthetic isolates.</li></ul><p style="margin:0;">Pectin-based gummy. Vegan, non-GMO, third-party tested. No stimulant laxatives, no harsh chemicals, no senna or magnesium.</p></div></div></div>
      <div class="mt-faq-item"><button class="mt-faq-q">I've already tried probiotics and they didn't work — how is this different?</button><div class="mt-faq-a"><p style="padding-top:4px;">Probiotics work on the colon — six feet downstream from your actual problem. GLP-1s slow the STOMACH. Motilli's apigenin is the first natural prokinetic formulated specifically to wake up stomach motility. You're targeting the right organ.</p></div></div>
      <div class="mt-faq-item"><button class="mt-faq-q">Can I take this alongside Miralax, magnesium, or fiber while I switch?</button><div class="mt-faq-a"><p style="padding-top:4px;">Yes. Most of our users taper off their old stack within 2–3 weeks once Motilli starts working. No interactions.</p></div></div>
      <div class="mt-faq-item"><button class="mt-faq-q">Does it work for diarrhea too, or just constipation?</button><div class="mt-faq-a"><p style="padding-top:4px;">Yes. Motilli normalizes digestion in both directions — the FOS fiber draws moisture when you're constipated and stabilizes transit time when you're loose. It's a regulator, not a one-way laxative.</p></div></div>
      <div class="mt-faq-item"><button class="mt-faq-q">I'm about to start my first GLP-1 shot — can I take Motilli preemptively?</button><div class="mt-faq-a"><p style="padding-top:4px;">Absolutely — many users start 5–7 days before their first injection. This gives apigenin a head start on supporting stomach function before the medication kicks in.</p></div></div>
      <div class="mt-faq-item"><button class="mt-faq-q">How do I take it? And for how long?</button><div class="mt-faq-a"><p style="padding-top:4px;">2 gummies daily, about 30 minutes before your biggest meal. Take Motilli for as long as you're on your GLP-1 — the side effects persist as long as the medication does.</p></div></div>
      <div class="mt-faq-item"><button class="mt-faq-q">When will I actually feel the difference?</button><div class="mt-faq-a"><p style="padding-top:4px;">Most users notice reduced sulfur burps within 3–5 days. Easier bowel movements within the first week. Full digestive reset within 2–4 weeks.</p></div></div>
      <div class="mt-faq-item"><button class="mt-faq-q">What happens if I stop taking it?</button><div class="mt-faq-a"><p style="padding-top:4px;">As long as you're still on a GLP-1, the side effects will return when Motilli clears your system. Motilli is a daily support supplement, not a one-time cure — that's why we offer the subscription option.</p></div></div>
      <div class="mt-faq-item"><button class="mt-faq-q">Is it safe for people with heart/kidney/diabetes conditions?</button><div class="mt-faq-a"><p style="padding-top:4px;">Motilli is formulated from natural whole-food extracts. However, if you have a specific health condition, always check with your doctor. Our support team can send a copy of the supplement facts on request.</p></div></div>
      <div class="mt-faq-item"><button class="mt-faq-q">Is this safe with Levothyroxine or other thyroid medication?</button><div class="mt-faq-a"><p style="padding-top:4px;">Yes, but always take Motilli at least 4 hours apart from Levothyroxine since any supplement with minerals can reduce absorption.</p></div></div>
      <div class="mt-faq-item"><button class="mt-faq-q">What if it doesn't work for me?</button><div class="mt-faq-a"><p style="padding-top:4px;">90-day full money-back guarantee. Email us for a refund — no questions, no ship-back required. The risk is ours.</p></div></div>
      <div class="mt-faq-item"><button class="mt-faq-q">How fast is shipping?</button><div class="mt-faq-a"><p style="padding-top:4px;">Orders ship same or next business day from our US facility. Standard delivery is 3–5 business days. Free over $45.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

